# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD starts httpd (`httpd -k start`) in the background and then
# execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * httpd is ALREADY RUNNING with the vulnerable config when the agent starts,
#     making the "fixed config but never restarted" case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting httpd cannot kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART httpd — the running server keeps
# the vulnerable config in memory until restarted.
